   q('Which muscle’s activity distinguishes a Duchenne smile from a posed smile?',['Orbicularis oris, closing the lips','Zygomatic major alone','Corrugator, lowering the brow','Orbicularis oculi, around the eyes'],3,'Both smiles raise the mouth corners through zygomatic major; the Duchenne smile also involves orbicularis oculi around the eyes.',['Orbicularis oris surrounds the mouth and is not the Duchenne marker.','Zygomatic major is active in both smiles.','Corrugator lowers the brow in frowning.','Correct: orbicularis oculi produces the eye crinkle of a Duchenne smile.'],'The mouth alone cannot tell you which type of smile you are seeing.')
